 "in_use_summary_en": "",
 "missing_en": "",
 "summary_en": "I found no public sign that South Ostrobothnia (Hyvaep) or Tays runs this. Hyvaep's radiology page says the X-ray report goes back to the treating doctor. Pirha's lung cancer pathway follows the usual route instead: the GP sends a referral, the hospital handles it in 1–2 working days, and CT usually follows within a week of that. On the effect, a 2023 randomised trial in Thorax (London, 49 lung cancers) found that reading primary-care chest X-rays while the patient waited cut the median time from X-ray to diagnosis from 63 to 32 days, a saving of 31 days.",
 "unanswered_en": "A final search for reporting radiographers who read chest X-rays in the county turned up nothing new, and I did not find Hyvaep's referral instructions for professionals or any local decision on this measure.",
